# Model-signing PRIVATE keys (scripts/ml/sign-model-artifact.ts). The trust store
# under artifacts/security/ holds public keys and IS committed on purpose — it is
# the operator's declaration of which signers may ship models. The private half
# must never be.
/.soterai/model-signing/
*.signing-key.pem
operator-signing-key.pem*

# Host-test scaffolding: dist-test is a build output, .vscode-test is a ~350MB
# downloaded VS Code the host suite launches. Both are regenerable.
packages/vscode-extension/dist-test/
packages/vscode-extension/.vscode-test/

# Compiled output of the n8n node's in-package test suite. `node --test` only
# discovers tests when cwd is inside the directory, so the suite is compiled
# here first; the TypeScript sources under test/ are what get reviewed.
packages/integrations/n8n/test-build/

SOTERAI-TEST-SECRETS.env
*.backup-pre-*
# Enumerating backup spellings has now lost this race three times. `.env.backup-*`
# missed `.env.pre-v14.bak`; the `.env*.bak` written to fix that missed
# `.env.bak.pre-v12`, because there the suffix lands AFTER `.bak` so `.bak` is not
# the final extension -- and that file sat untracked-but-addable on a public repo
# holding the same live DATABASE_URL, NEXTAUTH_SECRET and pepper values as .env.
# A rotated env gets whatever name the person rotating it typed, so match the
# shape instead: everything .env* is secret by default, and the tracked templates
# are re-admitted by name. A new backup is then ignored without anyone thinking
# about it, and a new template has to be added deliberately.
.env*
!.env*.example

# Generated ML artifacts, ignored by shape for the same reason as the envs above:
# `git add -A` should not be able to do something irreversible. No .npy or .npz has
# ever been tracked, and the embedding dumps under artifacts/ml-v2/ run 176-211 MB
# each -- 1.2 GB in total, every one of them past GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, and
# all of them regenerable by the training scripts. Output, not source.
*.npy
*.npz
artifacts/ml-v2/train-index-*.json
*-train-bundle.zip
# soterai-train-bundle.zip (11.8 MB) was committed deliberately, and the glob above
# swallows it. Re-admit it by name so a delete-and-re-add cannot lose it, the same
# way the .env templates are re-admitted.
!soterai-train-bundle.zip
soter-edge-test-out/
